., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITA TEIJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITAYAMA MASAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITA, TEIJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITAYAMA, MASAO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A colorless, transparent soda-lime silica glass which retains a high light transmittance in the visible region and absorbs ultraviolet; and a glass bottle which is obtained by molding the glass and enables the contents to look beautiful and to be prevented from suffering changes caused by ultraviolet, e.g., coloration, discoloration, fading, deterioration of flavor, etc.  The glass is characterized by having a composition containing 0.15 to 0.4 wt.% SO3, 0.2 to 1 wt.% cerium oxide (in terms of CeO2), 0.01 to 0.08 wt.% Fe2O3, 0 to 0.008 wt.% FeO, 0.01 to 0.08 wt.% manganese oxide (in terms of MnO), and 0 to 0.0005 wt.% cobalt oxide (in terms of CoO).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Verre sodo-calcique transparent incolore présentant une transmittance élevée de la lumière dans la zone visible et absorbant les ultraviolets; bouteille en verre fabriquée par moulage de ce verre et permettant à son contenu de conserver ses caractéristiques esthétiques et de lui éviter de subir des modifications provoquées par les ultraviolets, telles que la coloration, la décoloration, la dégradation ou la détérioration du goût. Ce verre est caractérisé par une composition contenant 0,15 à 0,4 % en poids de SO3, 0,2 à 1 % en poids d'oxyde de cérium (CeO2), 0,01 à 0,08 % en poids de Fe2O3, 0 à 0,008 % de FeO, 0,01 à 0,08 % en poids d'oxyde de manganèse (MnO) et 0 à 0,0005 % en poids d'oxyde de cobalt (CoO).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>